what this establishes
  The middle rung of the ladder is a real rung: the unstructured
  generator separates it from admissibility in most of its models.
  It is EMPTY on the real table and on both structured generators, and
  the union-graph criterion says why in a way that can be rechecked on
  any future cost table in one sweep.

  The design consequence, stated as a consequence and not as a rule:
  where the criterion is clean, a canon that required only 'never
  select a dominated arm' would get order-consistency for free, and a
  canon that required order-consistency would be asking for nothing
  extra. The two are only worth distinguishing where it is dirty.
